<div id="ImplementationContent" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiContent" data-tchmi-top="0" data-tchmi-left="0" data-tchmi-width="100" data-tchmi-width-unit="%" data-tchmi-min-width="916" data-tchmi-height="1217">
<div id="ImplementationHeadline" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.Beckhoff.TcHmiTextblock" data-tchmi-left="32" data-tchmi-top="16" data-tchmi-height="32" data-tchmi-right="16" data-tchmi-text="Implementation" data-tchmi-word-wrap="True">
<script data-tchmi-target-attribute="data-tchmi-class-names" type="application/json">
[
  "headline-2"
]
</script>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationContainer" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiContainer" data-tchmi-left="16" data-tchmi-top="64" data-tchmi-right="16" data-tchmi-min-width="884" data-tchmi-height="1137">
<script data-tchmi-target-attribute="data-tchmi-class-names" type="application/json">
[
  "background-container"
]
</script>
<div id="ImplementationDescription" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="24" data-tchmi-height="120" data-tchmi-right="24">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">The setter of <code style="font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px;">MyAttribute</code> creates a <code style="font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px;">TcHmi.ObjectResolver</code> with the control as parent and the type of the attribute. The resolver replaces each symbol expression with the current value of its symbol and calls the watch callback whenever one of them changes. When a spinbox of MyControl changes, its event handler writes a changed copy of the value and names the changed property as dirty path. The resolver writes it to the symbol if the expression uses <code style="font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 14px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px;">BindingMode=TwoWay</code> and reports the new value to the watch callback.</p>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationSetterText" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="160" data-tchmi-height="48" data-tchmi-width="528">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: bold;">1. Create and watch the resolver</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 24px;">The setter creates a resolver for the new value and registers its watch.</p>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationSetterCode" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="216" data-tchmi-height="228" data-tchmi-width="528">
<pre style="margin: 0; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 16px; overflow: hidden; background: rgba(30, 36, 48, 1); color: rgba(214, 222, 235, 1); border-radius: 4px; font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;">public <span style="color: rgba(121, 184, 255, 1);">setMyAttribute</span>(valueNew) {
    const resolver = <span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">new TcHmi.ObjectResolver</span>(valueNew, {
        parentControl: this,
        type: this.getAttributeDescription('MyAttribute')?.type,
    });
    this.__objectResolvers.set('MyAttribute', {
        resolver: resolver,
        watchCallback: this.__onMyAttributeWatchCallback,
        watchDestroyer: <span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">resolver.watch</span>(
            this.__onMyAttributeWatchCallback),
    });
}</pre>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationWatchText" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="468" data-tchmi-height="48" data-tchmi-width="528">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: bold;">2. Take over the resolved value</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 24px;">The watch callback stores each resolved value and updates the spinboxes.</p>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationWatchCode" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="524" data-tchmi-height="109" data-tchmi-width="528">
<pre style="margin: 0; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 16px; overflow: hidden; background: rgba(30, 36, 48, 1); color: rgba(214, 222, 235, 1); border-radius: 4px; font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;">protected <span style="color: rgba(121, 184, 255, 1);">__onMyAttributeWatchCallback</span>(data) {
    // ...
    this.__myAttributeValue = data.value;
    this.__processMyAttribute();
}</pre>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationAttachText" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="657" data-tchmi-height="48" data-tchmi-width="528">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: bold;">3. Connect the spinboxes</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 24px;">Each spinbox passes the property it edits and its new value on.</p>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationAttachCode" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="713" data-tchmi-height="143" data-tchmi-width="528">
<pre style="margin: 0; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 16px; overflow: hidden; background: rgba(30, 36, 48, 1); color: rgba(214, 222, 235, 1); border-radius: 4px; font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;">public <span style="color: rgba(121, 184, 255, 1);">__attach</span>() {
    TcHmi.EventProvider.register(
        `${this.getId()}.SpinboxInput_number1.onValueChanged`,
        () =&gt; this.__writeMyAttributeProperty(
            'number1', this.__spinBoxNumber1?.getValue()),
    );
}</pre>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationWriteText" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="880" data-tchmi-height="48" data-tchmi-width="528">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: bold;">4. Write the change back</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 24px;">A changed copy and its dirty path go to <code style="font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07); padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 3px;">write</code>, which updates TwoWay symbols.</p>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationWriteCode" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.System.TcHmiHtmlHost" data-tchmi-left="24" data-tchmi-top="936" data-tchmi-height="177" data-tchmi-width="528">
<pre style="margin: 0; height: 100%; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 16px; overflow: hidden; background: rgba(30, 36, 48, 1); color: rgba(214, 222, 235, 1); border-radius: 4px; font-family: Consolas, 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 13px; line-height: 17px;">protected <span style="color: rgba(121, 184, 255, 1);">__writeMyAttributeProperty</span>(property, value) {
    const resolverInfo = this.__objectResolvers.get('MyAttribute');
    // ...
    const valueNew = {
        ...this.__myAttributeValue,
        [property]: value,
    };
    <span style="background: rgba(46, 160, 67, 0.45); border-radius: 3px;">resolverInfo.resolver.write</span>(valueNew, [property]);
}</pre>
</div>
<div id="ImplementationMyControlLabel" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.Beckhoff.TcHmiTextblock" data-tchmi-left="600" data-tchmi-top="160" data-tchmi-height="24" data-tchmi-width="260" data-tchmi-text="MyControl" data-tchmi-word-wrap="False">
<script data-tchmi-target-attribute="data-tchmi-class-names" type="application/json">
